//
// Probe: which of the reference's 42 `dt` constants can a Bund program
// actually produce?
//
// RFC-0001 carries several negative claims — that `Val::Token` and four `dt`
// constants have no writer, that `cmp` is the unreachable ordering path. Each
// was established by grepping for callers, and that method has produced a
// false negative in three consecutive reviews: `Value::exit` (the parser
// calls it), `impl Iterator` (six `for … in` loops), `q` (every arithmetic
// operator).
//
// So this probe enumerates in the POSITIVE direction. It constructs one value
// of every `dt` a program can reach and pins the result. A constant absent
// from the capture is not thereby proven dead — the enumeration may simply not
// have found the word — but it is evidence of a different kind from a grep,
// and it is the kind that would have caught all three misses above.
//
// Three categories result, not two. `time.now` reaches TIME(13) and is
// deliberately absent: a clock reading differs between runs, so the capture
// refuses it. Reachable and unpinnable is its own answer, and the enumeration
// records it here rather than losing it.
//
"probe: one value per reachable dt" println
42                          debug.display_stack drop  // INTEGER 2
1.5                         debug.display_stack drop  // FLOAT 3
true                        debug.display_stack drop  // BOOL 1
"s"                         debug.display_stack drop  // STRING 4
'lit'                       debug.display_stack drop  // STRING 4 — note, not LITERAL 5
nodata                      debug.display_stack drop  // NODATA 97
"null" json                 debug.display_stack drop  // JSON 24
"null" json json.to_value   debug.display_stack drop  // NONE 0
list                        debug.display_stack drop  // LIST 9
dict                        debug.display_stack drop  // MAP 11
valuemap                    debug.display_stack drop  // VALUEMAP 30
metrics                     debug.display_stack drop  // METRICS 16
lambda                      debug.display_stack drop  // LAMBDA 17
`x                          debug.display_stack drop  // PTR 7
1 2 pair                    debug.display_stack drop  // PAIR 10
conditional                 debug.display_stack drop  // CONDITIONAL 29
"x" convert.to_textbuffer   debug.display_stack drop  // TEXTBUFFER 22
class                       debug.display_stack drop  // CLASS 31
1.0 2.0 complex             debug.display_stack drop  // CFLOAT 15
